CLASS com/corrodinggames/rts/gameFramework/k/k com/corrodinggames/rts/gameFramework/path/Path
	COMMENT Path - one requested/solved path (base class of FlowFieldPath). Fields: engine (PathEngine), id (unique id from the static nextId counter; printed by the debug logs), createdFrame (GameEngine frame the Path was constructed on), startX/startY/endX/endY (tile coords; PathSolver clips them to the map), targetHeight (Float), endRadius (goal is reached within this many tiles), movementType, avoidTightSpaces / requiredClearance (p/q - the clearance weighting and the minimum clearance in the A* cost function), nodes (LinkedList of PathSolverNode, compressed when sent over the network), terrainCost/unitBlocked/unitInfluence/groupIds/clearanceCost (cached copies of the MapCosts grids, filled by e() and released by f()), allowLowPriorityCosts/r etc. Behaviour/state fields: lowPriority (doubles allowedDelay), allowedDelay (the frame budget before a(PathEngine) hands the path to a blocking solve; printed in PathEngine.f() as "allowedDelay:"), remainingTime (counts down by the frame time in PathEngine.d(float)), hasResult (set when the grid was solved or the path arrived over the network), cancelled (set by PathEngine when a path is abandoned) and cancelRequested (volatile-ish flag checked in PathSolver.e()/g() to abort a running solve). Still obfuscated: k (boolean turn-cost mode passed to a(MovementType,short,short,Float,boolean)) and n/m reuse. [field names verified from code + PathEngine string literals]
